{"name":"Knitting Needles","hex":"#c3c1bc","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"knitting needles","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of knitting needle"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/knitting_needles"}],"entries":[{"title":"Knitting needle","blocks":[{"text":"A knitting needle or knitting pin is a tool in hand-knitting to produce knitted fabrics. They generally have a long shaft and taper at their end, but they are not nearly as sharp as sewing needles. Their purpose is two-fold. The long shaft holds the active (unsecured) stitches of the fabric, to prevent them from unravelling, whereas the tapered ends are used to form new stitches. Most commonly, a new stitch is formed by inserting the tapered end through an active stitch, catching a loop of fresh yarn and drawing it through the stitch; this secures the initial stitch and forms a new active stitch in its place. In specialized forms of knitting the needle may be passed between active stitches being held on another needle, or indeed between/through inactive stitches that have been knit previously."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Knitting_needles_2.jpg/330px-Knitting_needles_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Knitting_needle","wikidata":"Q1440357"},{"title":"Knitting","blocks":[{"text":"Knitting is the process of interlooping yarn to create textile fabric made of interconnected loops, done by hand, machine or both."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Oma_strickt_Str%C3%BCmpfe.jpg/330px-Oma_strickt_Str%C3%BCmpfe.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Knitting","wikidata":"Q193188"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Pink_knitting_in_front_of_pink_sweatshirt.JPG/500px-Pink_knitting_in_front_of_pink_sweatshirt.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Pink_knitting_in_front_of_pink_sweatshirt.JPG/1280px-Pink_knitting_in_front_of_pink_sweatshirt.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Pink_knitting_in_front_of_pink_sweatshirt.JPG/500px-Pink_knitting_in_front_of_pink_sweatshirt.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A little dexterity is helpful in working with knitting needles ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APink_knitting_in_front_of_pink_sweatshirt.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Straight_knitting_needles.JPG/500px-Straight_knitting_needles.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Straight_knitting_needles.JPG/1280px-Straight_knitting_needles.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Straight_knitting_needles.JPG/500px-Straight_knitting_needles.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Straight knitting needles in a variety of sizes and materials. Different materials have varying amounts of friction, and are suitable for different yarn types.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStraight_knitting_needles.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Puikot.jpg/500px-Puikot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Puikot.jpg/500px-Puikot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Flexi single-pointed needles. The upper one is constructed from an interchangeable circular knitt